{"files":[{"content":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint A[1000][1000];\nint ps[1010][1010];\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nstatic ll countBand(int m, int j, int l, int k, unordered_map<ll, ll>& h) {\n  h.clear();\n  h[0] = 1;\n  ll s = 0;\n  ll ans = 0;\n  for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\n    s += ps[i][l] - ps[i][j - 1];\n    ans += h.find(s - k) != h.end() ? h[s - k] : 0;\n    h[s]++;\n  }\n  return ans;\n}\n\nll solve(int m, int n, int k) {\n  for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\n    for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n      ps[i][j] = A[i - 1][j - 1] + ps[i][j - 1];\n    }\n  }\n\n  ll ans = 0;\n  const ll estimatedWork = static_cast<ll>(m) * n * (n + 1) / 2;\n  if (estimatedWork < 16384) {\n    unordered_map<ll, ll> h;\n    for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n      for (int l = j; l <= n; l++) {\n        ans += countBand(m, j, l, k, h);\n      }\n    }\n  } else {\n#pragma omp parallel num_threads(4) reduction(+ : ans)\n    {\n      unordered_map<ll, ll> h;\n#pragma omp for schedule(dynamic, 1)\n      for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n        for (int l = j; l <= n; l++) {\n          ans += countBand(m, j, l, k, h);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n  int k, m, n;\n  cin >> k >> m >> n;\n  memset(A, 0, sizeof A);\n  memset(ps, 0, sizeof ps);\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\n      cin >> A[i][j];\n\n  cout << solve(m, n, k) << endl;\n  return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/main.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"Dynamically sharing independent column bands across at most four OpenMP workers should reduce runtime for larger inputs while per-worker frequency maps and a 64-bit reduction preserve exact counts. A work estimate leaves small inputs on the serial path to avoid parallel startup overhead.","notes":"This isolates band-level work sharing and scheduling; both paths use the same band-counting routine. No performance result is assumed.","sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Factor the per-band prefix-sum frequency count into a shared routine, then dynamically schedule outer column-band groups across up to four OpenMP workers with a private map per worker and a 64-bit sum reduction.","Keep small estimated workloads serial to limit parallel overhead."]}